    },
    {
      "source": "S8",
      "quote": "Item B-1.8: Excavating trenches of required width for pipes cables etc. ... ORDINARY ROCK: -"
    }
  ],
  "answer": "The basic rate for excavating a trench for a pipe of 150 mm diameter (which falls in the 80 mm‑300 mm range) in ordinary rock up to 1.5 m depth is Rs 429.00 per metre [S3]. Because the trench depth is 2.5 m, which exceeds 1.5 m but does not exceed 3 m, an extra of 104 % is applied over the basic rate [S1]. The extra amount is 429.00 × 104 % = Rs 446.16 per metre. Adding this to the basic rate gives a total rate of Rs 429.00 + Rs 446.16 = Rs 875.16 per metre. This rate includes the complete excavation work (labour and material) for ordinary rock as defined in Item B‑1.8 [S8].",
  "missing": ""
}

